%S A400469 1,0,-1,-1,0,1,1,2,3,1,4,5,1,-4,-5,-1,4,3,-1,2,3,1,4,5,9,4,-5,-1,4,3,
%T A400469 7,10,3,13,16,29,13,-16,-29,-13,16,29,13,42,29,-13,16,29,13,-16,-3,
%U A400469 -19,-16,-35,-19,16,35,51,16,67,51,118,169,51,-118,-67,-185
%N A400469 Deterministic version of the random Fibonacci sequence, with signs from A076478 and the seed as (1,0).
%C A400469 Viswanath's random Fibonacci sequence flips a fair coin for each sign. Reading the signs off one fixed word instead gives a single integer sequence, and A076478 is normal in base 2, so every finite sign pattern still occurs with the frequency a coin would give it. Digit A076478(n-2) drives step n, with "1" adding and "0" subtracting.
%H A400469 Jwalin Bhatt, <a href="/A400469/b400469.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A400469 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/RandomFibonacciSequence.html">Random Fibonacci Sequence</a>
%H A400469 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random_Fibonacci_sequence">Random Fibonacci sequence</a>
%F A400469 For n>=2: a(n) = a(n-1) + a(n-2) if A076478(n-2) = 1, otherwise a(n-1) - a(n-2).
%F A400469 Conjecture: lim_{n->oo} |a(n)|^(1/n) = 1.1319882487943... (A078416), Viswanath's constant.
%e A400469 A076478 begins 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 1, 0, 1, 1, 0, ..., so the signs applied at steps n = 2, 3, 4, ... are -, +, -, -, -, +, +, -, +, +, -, ...
%e A400469 a(2) = a(1) - a(0) = 0 - 1 = -1, since A076478(0) = 0.
%e A400469 a(3) = a(2) + a(1) = -1 + 0 = -1, since A076478(1) = 1.
%e A400469 a(4) = a(3) - a(2) = -1 + 1 = 0, since A076478(2) = 0.
%e A400469 a(5) = a(4) - a(3) = 0 + 1 = 1, since A076478(3) = 0.
%t A400469 Module[{c = Flatten[Array[Rest@IntegerDigits[# + 1, 2] &, 30]], a}, a[n_] := a[n] = If[n <= 1, 1-n, a[n-1] + (2*c[[n-1]] - 1)*a[n-2]]; Array[a, 67, 0]]
%o A400469 (Python)
%o A400469 from itertools import count, islice, product
%o A400469 def A076478():  return (b for k in count(1) for v in product((0, 1), repeat=k) for b in v)
%o A400469 def A400469(n_terms):
%o A400469     a, d = [1, 0], list(islice(A076478(), n_terms))
%o A400469     for n in range(2, n_terms):
%o A400469         a.append(a[n-1] + a[n-2] if d[n-2] else a[n-1] - a[n-2])
%o A400469     return a
%o A400469 print(A400469(67))
%Y A400469 Cf. A000045, A076478, A078416, A400370, A400405.
